# countryball-map-story fix log

## epoch 0 (2026-11-23): created from a reference reel
Made by Claude from the rea-video breakdown of references/vod.mp4 (115.1 s, 576 x 1024, 30 fps: a countryball history story on a real map, 45 shots (22.9 cuts a minute, mean 2.6 s), 2D cut-out animation 88% plus a 3D night cutaway 12%; a male TTS narrator (about 128 Hz, 2.1 to 2.3 words a second) carries 75% of the voice and two character voices 25%; stock-style music bed at 112 bpm (F major), section changes at 50.5, 54.5, 58.5, 87.5 and 91.5 s; 7 sound effects (dings and a pop, mostly on titles)), see reference-lab/runs/vod/analysis-claude (survey + review by Claude), reference-lab/runs/vod/crops, sheets/contact.jpg + contact2.jpg + look1/look2.jpg, and reference-lab/refs/vod.
What was taken from the reference:
- Look (measured with rea-video's style aspect and tools/oklch_colours.py): steel-blue sea (L 0.54, C 0.08, hue 233) with a pale coast halo (L 0.60, C 0.07, hue 216 to 232); every country NOT in the story pale beige (L 0.78 to 0.80, C 0.05, hue 85); each country in the story filled with its flag's main colour at map strength: saffron orange (L 0.70, C 0.145, hue 66), green (L 0.57 to 0.62, C 0.10, hue 150 to 154), red (L 0.50 to 0.53, C 0.15 to 0.165, hue 25); warm near-black ink (L 0.13 to 0.19, C 0.03, hue 21); off-white text (L 0.97, C 0.02 to 0.04, hue 107); amber keywords (L 0.76, C 0.156, hue 61). Flat fills 82%, gentle gradients 11%, held frames 52% (limbs on twos), detail 3.78, no pixel grid; a low-contrast crumpled-paper texture over land and sea; 2 px coast line, no border lines (fills alone separate countries).
- Characters: flag-balls (the country's real flag in a circle, 5 px ink outline, big white eyes with lids and brows, small mouth, noodle arms with mitten hands in a flag-derived skin colour, contact shadow); power shown as size (one ball swells to about 3x).
- Signature: a wooden plank sign on a post planted in the disputed land whose one word changes through the story; the last change is the ending.
- Type: hand-lettered rounded uppercase titles (off-white, dark outline and shadow, slightly rotated) in the top third -> "Segoe Print" bold; letter-spaced serif map labels in dark brown -> Georgia 600; captions: short white phrases (3 to 4 words), dark shadow, numbers in amber, at about 74% of the height.
- Props: portrait medallions (archival photos in a ring: replaced by generic silhouettes, no likeness), papers with red seals, rolled messages on dotted routes, small flags on poles (a white flag for surrender), dashed movement arrows, a crowd of small helmeted balls, a flashback shown as a washed-out tint.
- Structure as 14 topic-free beats from the reference's narrative line: hook (the claim in one image, sign + title with place and year) -> setup (ball dialogue: ask and refuse) -> flashback (washed tint) -> word (first sign change) -> cost (human-scale detail) -> pressure (years, arrows) -> ally (another map, refusal) -> odds (size as power, ratio title) -> order (leader medallion, message route, quote title) -> event (crowd marching or fills changing, two labels) -> collapse (duration title, white flag; music payoff) -> moment (dark quiet night scene, one gesture) -> aftermath (iris back to the bright map, years later) -> payoff (the hook's composition, last sign change).
- Sound: narrator brian (deep American narrator, dry), ball voices adam / harry / roger, 5 to 8 ball lines of at most 6 words; music Suspenseful, Driving at 102 to 122 bpm (measured 112), payoff_shot = the collapse; about 1 effect per shot (pop on titles and the sign's word, knock on the sign, whoosh on map jumps and the iris).
Template choices that are not in the reference:
- The 3D night cutaway becomes a 2D "night" background (dark ground, a warm headlight pool, dust) with the two balls large: the same tonal shift without 3D.
- Character lines show as the engine's speech bubbles (the reference shows them as dash captions); the narrator gets the new phrase captions.
- 14 shots of about 6.4 s for a 90 s reel (the user's choice; the reference cuts every 2.6 s): each shot holds one view with a slow push-in and at most one camera move, and pops new things on its lines.
- The map is a kit helper (kit.map), not an asset: the asset validator rejects an asset that paints its whole box. An "overview" background calls kit.map so the kit's map is rendered and reviewed at the kit step, before any shot.
Engine changes (asked and approved by the user: "Add country fills", "Add 'phrases' mode"):
- engine/world.js: countries110 / countries50, every Natural Earth country's rings by name (reference-lab/tools/topo2world.py now writes them; shared arcs are simplified once so neighbours meet exactly); 2.2 MB (was 989 KB); the old land / border keys are byte-identical.
- stage_asset.html: a flat north-up Mercator view (v.proj 'merc') for h.geo, h.landPath, h.coastPath, h.borderPath (culled to the canvas through the current transform; rings crossing longitude 180 unwrapped once); h.countryPath(names, v, zoom) (Path2D of one or several countries; 'USSR', 'Yugoslavia', 'Czechoslovakia', 'Baltic states' as unions of their members; common aliases; an unknown name throws an error listing real names while validating); h.countryCentre(names); h.countryView(names, x, y, w, hgt). Checked by Claude: USSR, Ukraine, Europe and a globe view render right in 5 to 21 ms a frame.
- stage_asset.html: "captions: phrases": the narrator's line in chunks of up to 4 words (24 letters), white 58 px bold with a dark outline and shadow at y 1500, number words and digits in palette.accent.
Engine limits met on the way (not changed):
- No real photos for people: medallions hold a generic silhouette (plan rule: never a likeness).
- Speech bubbles for character lines (no dash captions).
First brief: "The fall of USSR" (90 s, 14 shots).

## epoch 1 (2026-11-23): fixes after reviewing the epoch-0 plan only (reels/ussr-e0plan-work/plan.json, brief "The fall of USSR"; the run stopped at the voice step: ElevenLabs HTTP 401 quota_exceeded, 0 credits; the user chose Kokoro voices)
Plan rejected once (digits in 5 lines: "in 1985", "in 1988", "1989 and 1991"), passed on the 2nd try: 14 shots, 188 words, VIEW / FILLS / BALLS / SIGN / TITLE lines in every idea. Epoch 0 got right: the beat order, the sign as the motif, republic fills in distinct colours, a night moment with the flag lowered, real dates (Gorbachev leader 11 March 1985, Belovezha Accords 8 December, resignation 25 December, dissolution 26 December 1991). Flaws seen -> fix:
- Hook a general statement ("did not fall overnight; its final border vanished") -> hook with a real number or a question; "hook: number or question" check.
- Union ball and member ball both "on" their country: kit.centre('USSR') is Russia's centre, so the two balls would sit on each other -> fixed left / right slots when one country contains the other or their centres are close.
- Balls at size 2.2 to 2.4 in ordinary shots (about 800 px) -> normal size 0.85 to 1.2 except the odds and moment beats.
- Ball flag given as prose in the asset states ("Soviet Union flag with red field and yellow emblem") -> the flag object everywhere, with real colours.
- A "Commonwealth of Independent States" ball speaking for Ukraine, and Gorbachev / Yeltsin in "cast" with the narrator's voice -> only countries and unions with a real flag are balls and speakers; people only as medallions, never in cast.
- Sign word "CONFEDERATION" made up for the middle of the story -> every WORD value is a name or status the place officially had, with its date.
- Titles over 18 characters and summary titles ("THREE FOUNDING REPUBLICS", "THE UNION UNRAVELS") -> count characters; a title is a date, count, name or short quote.
- Digits in lines -> years too written as words, digits only in titles.
- Voices named as ElevenLabs ids (brian, adam, harry, roger); with Kokoro they would all fall back to one default -> Kokoro ids (am_onyx narrator, am_adam, am_fenrir, am_michael), which the engine maps to the same kind of voice in every family.

## epoch 2 (2026-11-23): fixes after reviewing the epoch-1 reel (reels/ussr-e1-v1 88.7 s before the director round, reels/ussr-e1-v2 38.3 s after it; brief "The fall of USSR", 90 s, Kokoro voices; MiniMax $0.306 + Kokoro $0.001 = $0.307, 1041 s wall)
Grade (v2) vs vod: rhythm 0.19, rendering 0.21, colour 0.11; detail 6.7 vs 3.8, colours (95%) 94 vs 40, frame-to-frame change 0.69 vs 0.27, held frames 0% vs 52%, ground lightness 0.58 vs 0.54, tempo 146 vs 112 bpm.
Plan rejected once (broken JSON in asset states), passed on the 2nd try (179 words). 44 shot rejections, 9 shots shipped on "using the last one that runs"; shot 5 shipped black (a gradient fed an object, 3 tries).
Epoch 1 got right: the look reads at once as the reference's (steel-blue paper sea, beige real land with coast halos, Segoe Print titles with ink stroke, phrase captions with amber numbers), the flashback wash, generic medallion silhouettes, flag-balls with outlines, brows and noodle arms, the night moment with two large balls in a warm pool, the sign flipping its word, real dates (11 March 1985, 8 December, 26 December 1991, Kazakhstan the last to declare independence on 16 December, 11 republics in the CIS).
Flaws seen -> fix:
- ENGINE: the director wrote "who": "am_onyx" (the narrator's voice) for 8 shots; the engine dropped those lines and replaced each shot's lines with an empty list, so 8 of 14 shots went silent and v2 fell from 88.7 to 38.3 s -> asset_reel.mjs (approved by the user): a speaker given as a voice name maps back to its cast id, and a replacement that ends up empty is ignored and logged. Template: every "who" is a cast id; "the narrator (cast id "narrator") speaks with voice am_onyx".
- Wrong flags everywhere (the union ball in a red-yellow-red flag, a member ball in another country's tricolour): flags were invented per shot -> every flag is defined ONCE in style.flags and reaches every shot as kit.flags[id]; the asset draws a plain grey ball when no flag is passed.
- Soviet-era names ("Russian SFSR", "Ukrainian SSR") failed h.countryPath in 8 shots' first tries -> always today's Natural Earth names; the error message did its job but cost a retry each.
- The engine's pose sheet replaced the template's armL / armR params (shots passed no pose: rejected) -> the ball has exactly 5 named poses (arms_down, point, raise, hold_post, arms_up), named in its description and in every BALLS line, so the pose planner picks them.
- The union ball and the member ball on the same spot and the sign's post through a ball's face -> one fixed composition with the sign (plank x 396 to 684, y 706 to 818; balls at (279, 980) and (801, 980), the hold_post hand on the post); ball box widened to 640 so the hold_post hand reaches the post.
- Member fills drawn over the union while it still existed (half the union red, Russia green in the hook) -> a union is one fill until a member leaves.
- Invented "3 TO 1" odds -> the odds title compares the same real quantity for both sides with units; never an invented ratio.
- Titles written in words ("ELEVEN MARCH 1985", "TWENTY-SIX DECEMBER") -> dates and counts in digits on screen.
- Junk text ("ARCHIVAL REFORM ERA" under a timeline) -> the only text: title, at most 3 place labels, medallion names, the sign's word.
- Labels off the frame edge ("UKRAINE" at x -7, "LITHUANIA" at x -79, rejected in 4 shots) -> kit.label moves text inward to x 70 to 1010.
- Map too far out (the USSR fitted 980 px wide shows Africa to the Pacific) -> kit.view's default box 1500 wide: a wide country fills the width, cropped like the reference's maps.
- Too much texture and motion (detail 6.7 vs 3.8, 94 colours vs 40, change 0.69 vs 0.27) -> fine grain blotches 6 to 28 px at 2 to 5%, 40 wave marks, push-in 0.6% per second.
- Kit rejected once: night background too still (0.11 vs 0.2) -> the pool breathes, motes rise 25 to 45 px per second.
- Acting rejections in 9 shots -> a code recipe: expression changes at every line start, pose once in the middle.
- A medallion made into a third asset -> exactly 2 assets; asset states never wrapped in a "param" key.
Engine limits met: Kokoro's pitch spread 2.2 st (gate 4) is a flat delivery; held frames stay 0% because the host's neutral camera drift changes every frame.

## epoch 3 (2026-11-23): fixes after reviewing the epoch-2 reel (reels/ussr-e2-v2, brief "The fall of USSR", 90 s, Kokoro; MiniMax $0.350 + Kokoro $0.001 = $0.351, 94.5 s film, 797 s wall)
Grade vs vod: rhythm 0.31, rendering 0.23, colour 0.03 (was 0.11); cuts 8.3 vs 22.9 a minute (mean shot 6.75 vs 2.56 s), frame-to-frame change 0.41 vs 0.27, moving frames 0.24 vs 0.27, detail 7.4 vs 3.8, colours 87 vs 40, harmony now the same (complementary with extra hues), tempo 108 vs 112 bpm, ground lightness 0.49 vs 0.54.
Plan rejected once (Estonia, Lithuania and the USA speaking without cast entries), passed on the 2nd try (199 words); kit rejected once (sea and overview too flat: brightness std 4.5 vs 6, after epoch 2 made the texture finer); 47 shot rejections, 6 fallbacks (acting 1 beat short in 4, a big solid rectangle over the map in 1, a label "UNDEFINED" in 1). The director fix held: the revision kept every line (94.5 s).
Epoch 2 got right: the hook reads like the reference (the whole union one red fill on the real map, the sign "USSR" between two facing balls, title with the year in amber), flags defined once (Russia, Estonia, Lithuania right), the 5 named poses used, a real odds title (1989 census populations), the night moment with the flag change, phrase captions, real dates (16 November 1988, 25, 8 and 26 December 1991, since 1922).
Flaws seen -> fix:
- The union's flag drawn as red-yellow-red stripes (a one-colour field with an emblem) -> a one-colour field is ONE band with the emblem on top; never add stripes.
- Russia filled yellow (not in its flag) and the whole map yellow from shot 5 -> a fill is always a colour that is in the country's own flag.
- Balls cut off at the left edge in 4 shots (placed at kit.centre near the edge) and the slots ignored outside the hook -> every ball clamped whole inside the frame; the sign composition in EVERY shot with the sign.
- The same Eurasia view in 13 of 14 shots (the reference cuts to a new place every 2 to 3 s) -> FIT only the 1 to 3 countries a shot is about; only hook, setup, word and payoff use the stage view; a hard cut to a closer view on line 2 (raises cuts a minute toward the reference's).
- Sign word blank in the flashback and unreadable in the payoff ("COMMONWEALTH") -> always pass the word; WORD values at most 10 characters.
- Dates out of order (25 December, then 8 December, then 26 December) and "that night" on the wrong day (the flag came down on the 25th) -> time runs forward except in the flashback; "that night" means the shot's own date.
- "fifty-one and seven million" -> decimals spoken with "point".
- Summary title "THE BALTICS BREAK FREE" -> titles are dates, counts or place names; quotes only in the order beat.
- Ally beat invented (Russia asking Washington to save the union) -> the real request and the real answer, or a second pressure beat.
- "UNDEFINED" label -> kit text helpers draw nothing for a missing text.
- Acting rejections: the check counts distinct states minus one, so a 6.9 s shot at "acting beat: 4" needed 3 different states -> "acting beat: 7" (2 states up to 7 s, about the reference's 1 to 2 expressions per 2.5 s shot).
- Kit sea too flat after the finer grain -> the pool + 0.08 and the vignette - 0.11 stated (the grain stays fine).

## epoch 3 review (2026-11-23): the epoch-3 reel (reels/ussr-e3-v2, brief "The fall of USSR", 90 s, Kokoro; MiniMax $0.229 + Kokoro $0.001 = $0.230, 85.7 s film, 634 s wall); fixes not yet written (3-round limit reached, waiting for the user)
Grade vs vod: rhythm 0.39, rendering 0.32, colour 0.01 (best); cuts 9.8 vs 22.9 a minute, frame-to-frame change 0.84 vs 0.27, moving frames 0.68 vs 0.27, flat fills 0.67 vs 0.82, detail 8.5 vs 3.8, colours 88 vs 40, held frames 0 vs 0.52, ground lightness 0.55 vs 0.54, tempo 98 vs 112.
Plan and kit passed on the first try; 15 shot rejections (47 in epoch 2), 2 fallbacks (a full-frame rectangle over the map in shot 8, a label overlapping a "?" in shot 4).
Epoch 3 got: every ball whole inside the frame, the sign composition in every sign shot with a readable word (USSR -> SOVEREIGN), one red union fill, a closer Baltic view for the cost beat, a real Belovezha dialogue (Russia and Ukraine, Belarus with them), dates in order through December, the night moment, colour nearly the reference's.
Flaws still seen, with the fix to write next:
- Flags still wrong after two prose rules: the union ball red-yellow-red striped (a one-colour field), Estonia blue-white-green (blue-black-white), Belarus red-green (white-red-white in 1991) -> engine: real flag data (a table of flags by country name, with historic ones such as the USSR's) behind h.flag(name), so balls never depend on M3's memory of flags.
- Wrong numbers the director kept: "Russia had roughly sixteen million people" (about 148 million), the flag lowered "on twenty-six December" (25 December), "vanished in twenty-six days" (doubtful) -> engine: check the odds beat's numbers against the fact lookup, or a template rule that the odds numbers come from the reference text only.
- Too much motion and detail (change 0.84, moving 0.68, detail 8.5): the sea's texture reads as clouds again and every element moves -> state the texture as an image M3 cannot enlarge (blotch count and size limits), hold balls still between acting beats (bob 2 px), drop the wave marks.
- Still mostly one stage view (cuts 9.8 a minute; only the cost beat got a closer view; no "then FIT on line 2" cuts) -> make the closer view a per-beat requirement in the structure list.
